MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 09d9dd0205bab0640872e2256248d999, type: 3}
  m_Name: Backstory
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  _source: {fileID: 4900000, guid: 96f44f0c2089e5a489f96d2c855eece1, type: 3}
  _sourcePath: Assets/Leveraged Wars Story/2. Missions/M1-Tutorial/Backstory.md
  _warnings: []
  _lines:
  - Speaker: Bard
    Text: Hear ye, hear ye! Attend the noble tale
    WordsPerMinute: 0
    SpeakerSide: 1
    LeftName: Bard
    RightName: 
    LeftPortrait: {fileID: 7468356559241021412, guid: b23a63486994642469fcc255da0779d2,
      type: 3}
    RightPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  - Speaker: Bard
    Text: 'Of prince Julian,

      To good King Prinius and Freya born,

      True
      heir to all Aurelliam''s high throne.'
    WordsPerMinute: 0
    SpeakerSide: 1
    LeftName: Bard
    RightName: 
    LeftPortrait: {fileID: 7468356559241021412, guid: b23a63486994642469fcc255da0779d2,
      type: 3}
    RightPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  - Speaker: Bard
    Text: 'The royal hearth bestowed its richest gifts:

      Their noble spirit,
      beauty, health, and grace;

      And at his very birth, the falcon sang.'
    WordsPerMinute: 0
    SpeakerSide: 1
    LeftName: Bard
    RightName: 
    LeftPortrait: {fileID: 7468356559241021412, guid: b23a63486994642469fcc255da0779d2,
      type: 3}
    RightPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  - Speaker: Bard
    Text: 'He grew in strength; all beasts within the realm

      Gave heed unto
      their prince. The fiercest boars

      Of all Aurelliam came meek as lambs

      Upon
      his maiden hunt; and where he pissed,

      The sweetest roses burst in sudden
      bloom.'
    WordsPerMinute: 0
    SpeakerSide: 1
    LeftName: Bard
    RightName: 
    LeftPortrait: {fileID: 7468356559241021412, guid: b23a63486994642469fcc255da0779d2,
      type: 3}
    RightPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  - Speaker: Bard
    Text: 'He would have stayed among us, grown to rule,

      A king both hale
      and wise, whose gentle touch

      Had healed the sick throughout our troubled
      land.

      We weep for Prinius and Freya slain,

      Deceived, alas, by
      black betrayal''s snare.

      That poison, steeped in envy, struck them dead,

      And
      had undone young Julian as well,

      Had not the Faeries whisked him safe
      away.'
    WordsPerMinute: 0
    SpeakerSide: 1
    LeftName: Bard
    RightName: 
    LeftPortrait: {fileID: 7468356559241021412, guid: b23a63486994642469fcc255da0779d2,
      type: 3}
    RightPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  - Speaker: Bard
    Text: 'Within Queen Guenivere''s bright faery court,

      With hermits of a
      thousand years he learned,

      He diced with Death, and slew with naked
      hands

      A serpent rising full a hundred feet.

      Yet left the fairest
      princess of that shore,'
    WordsPerMinute: 0
    SpeakerSide: 1
    LeftName: Bard
    RightName: 
    LeftPortrait: {fileID: 7468356559241021412, guid: b23a63486994642469fcc255da0779d2,
      type: 3}
    RightPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  - Speaker: Bard
    Text: To seek Aurelliam, his home, once more.
    WordsPerMinute: 0
    SpeakerSide: 1
    LeftName: Bard
    RightName: 
    LeftPortrait: {fileID: 7468356559241021412, guid: b23a63486994642469fcc255da0779d2,
      type: 3}
    RightPortrait: {fileID: 0}
